<title>FRANCE: Havas boosted by CEP buy-out rumour.</title>
<headline>Havas boosted by CEP buy-out rumour.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Havas were up by nearly six percent in late Tuesday trading on rumours it would launch a buy-out bid on minorities in 73 percent-held unit CEP Communications.</p>
<p>Havas was up 22 francs at 395. CEP was suspended pending a statement at 400 francs.</p>
<p>Dealers said Havas would benefit from such an operation.  </p>
<p>There was no immediate comment at Havas nor at CEP.</p>
</text>
